Z||000000||gt boy||08-30-2001||10:59 PM||||i am planning on getting my gt lowered...how easy is it to do yourself??  how much do you end up saving by doing it yourself??<P>is there a kit that is better than others??? <P>how much of a drop is practical?? i will be using the stock rims for now on my 86 gt but plan on getting some 17"'s down the road ...do i need to plan ahead for the wheel change?<P>thanks in advance.||||reg||5
Z||000001||c m west||08-30-2001||11:06 PM||||if you want to cut the spring I can tell you exactly what need to be done||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDusty||08-30-2001||11:09 PM|||| As far as dropping your fiero...Eibach makes a great set of springs, but putting them on yourself is a real pain. You'll need a spring compressor to safely take them off without damaging something or someone. The whole process will probably take you 4 hours with the proper tools and not running into any snags. You can save about $100 doing it yourself...but once you realize what a task it is to do you'll realize that it is worth every penny to just have it done.<P>Dusty 86GT||||reg||6
Z||000003||gt boy||08-30-2001||11:15 PM||||c m west...where does it need to be cut...but will it ride the same as if you put in a lowering kit??||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||08-31-2001||12:34 AM||||The amount to cut varies depending on the suspension package in your Fiero.  Springs settle over their life a bit which may affect how much you need to cut.<P>Personally, I would measure, then cut, say 1/4 of a coil off both sides and measure again.  Repeat until desired drop is acheived.<P>2" and anything beyond that is getting crazy.  1" to 1-1/2" is a reasonable drop.<P>I went with 2" drop spindles from Street Dreams on the front, and 1" to 1-1/2" drop springs for the rear on mine.<P>Drop spindles maintain the suspension geometry, stock springs, and ride travels.  Not as cheap as cutting springs but something you may want to consider.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue4.gif">    <BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR><A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/tatooine/spielberg/241/" TARGET=_blank>Tigger's Fiero Page</A><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 08-31-2001).]||||reg||1
